    },
    {
      "id": "grecSMAE-53koVFSy1hLx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1843.1001092750862,
      "y": 1397.2109325676734,
      "width": 1121.5191650390625,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2075225952,
      "version": 508,
      "versionNonce": 1465869984,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787333852808,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Search — a user types \"cat videos\" in the search bar. What kind of database/index would actually serve this, and \nwhy would a normal SQL LIKE '%cat%' query be a terrible idea at scale?\n\n\ndisadvantages of LIKE '%cat%'\n- B-tree index therefore the entire table ie each row needs to be scanned which is called a full table scan\n- only performs exact matching cannot handle typos\n- fails to find content based on views and popularity\n- fails on synonms for the word cat like 'cats' or 'kittens'\n\nThe solution\n- elastic search (inverted index)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Search — a user types \"cat videos\" in the search bar. What kind of database/index would actually serve this, and \nwhy would a normal SQL LIKE '%cat%' query be a terrible idea at scale?\n\n\ndisadvantages of LIKE '%cat%'\n- B-tree index therefore the entire table ie each row needs to be scanned which is called a full table scan\n- only performs exact matching cannot handle typos\n- fails to find content based on views and popularity\n- fails on synonms for the word cat like 'cats' or 'kittens'\n\nThe solution\n- elastic search (inverted index)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FRFpf2jFzVLujt5hCAff_",
